# Build a Live Automation Monitoring Dashboard Using Java Spring Boot

## 1. Objective

Build a lightweight, standalone, real-time HTML dashboard to visualize test-generation and automation progress across individual skills and tasks.

The dashboard will provide testing teams with visibility into:
- Which skills are currently executing.
- Which skills have completed.
- Which skills are pending.
- Which skills have failed.
- Real-time progress of individual skills.
- Number of test cases generated.
- Execution activity and logs.
- Overall execution progress.

The solution must be generic, configurable, modular and reusable across multiple projects and testing teams.

IMPORTANT SCOPE:

For this iteration, implement ONLY the monitoring dashboard and its backend infrastructure.

Do not implement:
- Test-generation logic.
- AI/LLM integration.
- Spec-Driven Quality Engine.
- Testing Constitution.
- Quality gates.
- Actual test execution engines.
- Application-specific business logic.

The architecture should allow these capabilities to be integrated in future iterations without redesigning the dashboard.

