## 5. REST API Design

Implement versioned REST endpoints.

### Dashboard APIs

GET /api/v1/dashboard

Returns the complete current dashboard state.

GET /api/v1/projects

Returns registered projects.

GET /api/v1/runs

Returns execution runs.

GET /api/v1/runs/{runId}

Returns details of a particular execution.

GET /api/v1/skills

Returns registered skills.

GET /api/v1/health

Returns application health.

### Event APIs

POST /api/v1/events

Receives execution events.

GET /api/v1/runs/{runId}/events

Returns event history for an execution.

### Real-time API

GET /api/v1/stream

Establishes an SSE connection using Spring MVC SseEmitter.

The SSE implementation must:
- Support multiple concurrent browser clients.
- Broadcast updates to all relevant connected clients.
- Handle client disconnections.
- Remove completed or failed emitters.
- Send initial dashboard state when a client connects.
- Support heartbeat events.
- Handle reconnection through browser EventSource.
- Avoid unnecessary thread creation.
- Use a bounded event buffer where appropriate.

Use Last-Event-ID for event replay where practical.

