## 8. Dashboard UI Requirements

Build a professional engineering dashboard using HTML, CSS and vanilla JavaScript.

The dashboard should be visually clean, responsive and suitable for daily testing-team usage.

### A. Header

Display:
- Dashboard title: Live Automation Monitor.
- Project name.
- Application/service name.
- Execution run ID.
- Environment.
- Current server connection status.
- Last update timestamp.

### B. Overall Execution Summary

Display metric cards for:

- Total skills.
- Completed skills.
- Running skills.
- Failed skills.
- Pending skills.
- Overall progress percentage.
- Total generated test cases.
- Total execution duration.

All metrics must be calculated from actual backend state.

### C. Skill Execution Dashboard

Display each skill as an independent card.

Each card should contain:
- Skill ID.
- Skill name.
- Description.
- Execution status.
- Progress percentage.
- Progress bar.
- Start timestamp.
- End timestamp.
- Duration.
- Completed tasks.
- Total tasks.
- Generated test case count.
- Current activity message.
- Last updated timestamp.
- Error details if applicable.

Support:
- Expandable skill details.
- Filtering by status.
- Searching by skill name.
- Sorting by status and latest activity.

New skills must automatically appear when registered.

### D. Live Activity Stream

Create a chronological activity panel.

Examples:

- Specification analysis started.
- Specification analysis completed.
- Test plan generation started.
- 25 positive test cases generated.
- Negative scenario generation completed.
- Automation script generation failed.
- Execution retry initiated.

Each log entry should display:
- Timestamp.
- Skill name.
- Event type.
- Message.
- Severity.

Newest events should appear first.

Provide filters for:
- Skill.
- Status.
- Event type.
- Severity.

### E. Execution Details

Allow users to inspect:
- Current run details.
- Individual skill execution history.
- Generated artifact references.
- Error messages.
- Retry information.
- Execution start and completion times.

Do not expose sensitive execution data.

