## 17. Final Acceptance Criteria

The implementation is complete when:

- The Java Spring Boot application starts successfully.
- No Node.js runtime is required.
- No third-party frontend framework is required.
- Dashboard URL is displayed with the actual assigned port.
- Skills are dynamically configurable.
- Multiple runs can be tracked independently.
- Real incoming events update the dashboard immediately.
- SSE works with multiple connected browsers.
- Browser reconnection works.
- Latest execution state survives browser refresh.
- Execution state is restored after application restart.
- Activity logs display actual incoming events.
- Demo mode works separately.
- Automated tests pass.
- README documents the complete implementation.

IMPORTANT:

Keep this implementation focused exclusively on the Live HTML Automation Monitoring Dashboard.

Do not implement the future Quality Engineering Engine or any test-generation functionality.

Prioritize clean Java architecture, maintainability, modularity, reliability and future extensibility.
